{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-342697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y={x}^{2}+1$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{2}$ at the point where $x=1,$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}+1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot 2(1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\cdot 2 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342697" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-342697" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342697" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=3x-1$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ at the point where $x=-1,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3x-1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2$ and $x=-1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\cdot (3)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48763" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-48763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48763" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-313855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $x=2,$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-313855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-3{x}^{2}+8x-5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $x=2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (-3\\cdot (2)^{2}+8\\cdot (2)-5)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-313855" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-313855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-313855" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=2{x}^{3}-2x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1$ at the point where $x=-2,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{3}-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-2x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (6{x}^{2}-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=1$ and $x=-2,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =1\\cdot (6\\cdot (-2)^{2}-2)=22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48765" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-48765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10"] ["math" "22"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48765" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "22"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ at the point where $x=-1,$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}=3$ and $x=-1,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12(-1)^{3}+6(-1)^{2}) \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-6) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48770" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-48770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48770" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r=-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{3}$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\,(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }\\,(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{3}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot [-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})] \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-2) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342707" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-342707" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342707" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{6}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-48806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-313637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r=5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ evaluate $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}$ at that point.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-313637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (5\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot 5\\cdot (\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-313637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "cate