given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=-3$ and $\\theta =\\pi ,$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =(-3)\\cdot (-1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48801" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-48801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{2}"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-48801" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r=\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $\\theta =\\theta (t),$ and that $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=7$ at the point where $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\theta +6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}=7$ and $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6},$ and solve for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =7\\cdot (1-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{6})) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =7\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115772" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-115772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "21"] ["math" "24"] ["math" "26"] ["math" "28"] ["math" "32"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115772" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "28"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y={x}^{2}-6x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=2\\,\\text{cm}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{2}-6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}-6x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (2x-6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=3\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =3\\cdot (2\\cdot 2-6)\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72231" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-72231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "7\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "9\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72231" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+{x}^{2}] \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x+1}+2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3+1}+2(3)) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (\\frac{1}{4}+6) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{25}{4} \\\\  & =-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of $-25\\text{ }\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342740" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-342740" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342740" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-25"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=4{x}^{3}+16x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\text{cm}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4{x}^{3}+16x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{x}^{3}+16x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{3}+16x) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (12{x}^{2}+16).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =(-\\frac{1}{4})\\cdot (12\\cdot (3)^{2}+16)\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-115785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "-30\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "-33\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "-36\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-115785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-31\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=2\\,\\text{cm}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2}-3{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (4x-3{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=2$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(4\\cdot (2)-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s} \\\\  & =2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72227" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-72227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(8+2{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "-2(2+{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "2(2-8{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] ["math" "8-{e}^{2}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-72227" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2(8-3{e}^{2})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=\\sqrt{x+1}$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=3\\,\\,\\text{cm}.$\n\nThe $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\sqrt{x+1} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x+1}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}=-4\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}$ and $x=3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{3+1}} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the $y$-coordinate is changing at the rate of $-1\\text{ }\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342736" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5771dddcabec70c63c94800789cd91c2608b4f9b173a8216fece77d8ea31248"} {"question" "q-342736" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "q-342736" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/state.json" "file_sha256" "1a55fc858d89fbd527b2fd670225046ef25db70cd79790e52ef09274e5531c59"} {"question" "e-10899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=x^3+e^x$ for $x=x(t),$ and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2$ at the point where $x=1,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/example-10899.json" "file_sha256" "d41e5980f468c4e076a8cb1d789db785cf778209787ab42282d393a46d3d8155"} {"question" "e-10899" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & ={x}^{3}+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({x}^{3}+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}+{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2$ and $x=1,$ and solve for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3\\cdot {1}^{2}+{e}^{1}) \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (3+e) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{2}{3+e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/example-10899.json" "file_sha256" "d41e5980f468c4e076a8cb1d789db785cf778209787ab42282d393a46d3d8155"} {"question" "e-10901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $r=\\sin\\theta$ for $\\theta = \\theta(t),$ and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/example-10901.json" "file_sha256" "46006225d2ea4813ce82ad8978dd22122a99d661fef9f63b033d95f0afd1c172"} {"question" "e-10901" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(r) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}\\theta }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4},$ and solve for $\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}\\theta }{\\text{d}t} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/example-10901.json" "file_sha256" "46006225d2ea4813ce82ad8978dd22122a99d661fef9f63b033d95f0afd1c172"} {"question" "e-10902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=x+e^x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}.$ Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=5\\,\\textrm{cm}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/example-10902.json" "file_sha256" "0f32df4ed4000d69e441b2447479711c18fe4c3915701546936cf1cb8fde15a4"} {"question" "e-10902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =x+{e}^{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(y) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(x+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+{e}^{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\cdot (1+{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}=2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}$ and $x=5$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t} & =2(1+{e}^{5})\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060523/example-10902.json" "file_sha256" "0f32df4ed4000d69e441b2447479711c18fe4c3915701546936cf1cb8fde15a4"}] "usage" {"e-10901" [] "q-48806" [] "e-10902" [] "q-48765" [] "e-10899" []} "basis" 1931 "retractions" [[17592186097172 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nGiven that $y = 2x^{3} - 2x$ for $x = x(t)$, and that $\\frac{dx}{dt} = 1$ at the point where $x =-2$, find $\\frac{dy}{dt}$."] [17592186097175 :question/problem "Given that $r = \\cos θ$ for $θ = θ(t)$, and that $\\frac{dr}{dt} = \\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $θ = \\frac{π}{4}$, find $\\frac{dθ}{dt}$."] [17592186096302 :question/problem "Given that $y=x^3+e^x$ for $x=x(t)$, and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2$ at the point where $x=1$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}$."] [17592186096302 :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= x^{3} + e^{x} \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dt}(y) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(x^{3} + e^{x}) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= \\frac{dx}{dt} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(x^{3} + e^{x}) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= \\frac{dx}{dt} \\cdot (3x^{2} + e^{x})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d t}=2\n$$\n\nand $x=1$, and solve for\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 &= \\frac{dx}{dt} \\cdot (3 \\cdot 1^{2} + e^{1}) \\\\\n2 &= \\frac{dx}{dt} \\cdot (3 + e) \\\\\n\\frac{dx}{dt} &= \\frac{2}{3 + e}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096303 :question/problem "Given that $r=\\sin\\theta$ for $\\theta = \\theta(t)$, and that $\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}$ at the point where $\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}$, find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}$."] [17592186096303 :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr &= \\sin θ \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dt}(r) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(\\sin θ) \\\\\n\\frac{dr}{dt} &= \\frac{dθ}{dt} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dθ}(\\sin θ) \\\\\n\\frac{dr}{dt} &= \\frac{dθ}{dt} \\cdot \\cos θ\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d r}{\\textrm d t}=\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\nand solve for\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d \\theta}{\\textrm d t}\n$$\n\nWe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dr}{dt} &= \\frac{dθ}{dt} \\cdot \\cos θ \\\\\n\\sqrt{2} &= \\frac{dθ}{dt} \\cdot \\cos (\\frac{π}{4}) \\\\\n\\sqrt{2} &= \\frac{dθ}{dt} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\\n\\frac{dθ}{dt} &= \\sqrt{2} \\cdot \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\\n\\frac{dθ}{dt} &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186096304 :question/problem "A particle $P$ is moving along the curve $y=x+e^x$ such that the $x$-coordinate of $P$ is changing at the rate of $2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}$. Find the rate of change of the $y$-coordinate when $x=5\\,\\textrm{cm}$."] [17592186096304 :question/worked-solution "Differentiating the given relation with respect to $t$ using implicit differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= x + e^{x} \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dt}(y) &= \\frac{d}{dt}(x + e^{x}) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= \\frac{dx}{dt} \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(x + e^{x}) \\\\\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= \\frac{dx}{dt} \\cdot (1 + e^{x})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can substitute the given information\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d x}{\\textrm d t}=2 \\,\\textrm{cm}/\\textrm{s}\n$$\n\nand $x=5$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dt} &= 2(1 + e^{5})cm/s\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186095390 17592186095391 17592186095392 17592186095393 17592186095394 17592186095408 17592186095409 17592186095410 17592186095411 17592186095412] "immutable_fields" [[17592186095389 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095389 :answer-field/id] [17592186095389 :answer-field/key] [17592186095389 :answer-field/type] [17592186095407 :answer-field/correct] [17592186095407 :answer-field/id] [17592186095407 :answer-field/key] [17592186095407 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
